    "title": "USI hosts veteran support summit - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nEVANSVILLE, Ind. (WEHT) — An event to support veterans looking for work was held at the University of Southern Indiana.\nOver 60 veterans attended the INvet Summit looking to swap one uniform for another on Wednesday. Veterans from all branches as well as military spouses and families were encouraged to attend.\nOld National Bank and Toyota were some of the companies on site. Last year, the organization held 3 events across Indiana to help veterans in their job search.\nThey’ve already hosted 5 events this year and their next one is set for October.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "(WEHT) — An event to support veterans looking for work was held at the University of Southern Indiana. Over 60 veterans attended the INvet Summit looking to swap one uniform for another on Wednesday. Veterans from all branches as well as military spouses and families were encouraged to attend. Last year, the organization held 3 events across Indiana to help veterans in their job search. They’ve already hosted 5 events this year and their next one is set for October.",
